OL,3,AOpenAI unveils AI assistant 'dots'
OL,4,Awhile safety worries delay new model
OL,5,
OL,6,FOpenAI on Tuesday unveiled "dots," a
OL,7,Fnew artificial intelligence (AI)
OL,8,Fassistant they say can proactively
OL,9,Fcarry out tasks on a user's behalf.
OL,11,FAt its annual developer day in San
OL,12,FFrancisco, chief executive Sam Altman
OL,13,Freferred to "dots" as "remarkably
OL,14,Fcapable, always-on agents that can
OL,15,Fhandle really anything you can think
OL,16,Fof."
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790729294
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AOpenAI unveils AI assistant 'dots'
OL,4,Awhile safety worries delay new model
OL,5,
OL,6,FAt the same time, OpenAI president Greg
OL,7,FBrockman and other tech leaders held a
OL,8,Fmeeting with President Donald Trump as
OL,9,Fthe firm faces intense scrutiny after
OL,10,Finternal tests of its AI agents
OL,11,Frevealed unexpected and occasionally
OL,12,Fharmful actions.
OL,14,FDots, however, were pitched as brightly
OL,15,Fcoloured cute cartoons meant to
OL,16,Ffunction as digital assistants for
OL,17,Fpeople with busy lives.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/19
